# Resource Registry

Purpose:
  Central registry for all system resources. Enables self-updating
  knowledge, resource discovery, and future-proofing. Resources
  are versioned, indexed, and discoverable.

## Resource Types

SKILL:
  Engineering skills (L1-L5)
  Location: .sdd/skills/
  Registry: .sdd/skills/INDEX.sdd

TEMPLATE:
  Project structure templates
  Location: .sdd/templates/
  Registry: .sdd/templates/INDEX.sdd

WORKFLOW:
  Execution workflows
  Location: .sdd/workflows/
  Registry: .sdd/workflows/INDEX.sdd

COMMAND:
  CLI commands
  Location: .sdd/commands/
  Registry: .sdd/commands/INDEX.sdd

PATTERN:
  Resilience patterns
  Location: .sdd/patterns/
  Registry: .sdd/patterns/INDEX.sdd

DECISION:
  Decision records
  Location: .sdd/decisions/
  Registry: .sdd/decisions/INDEX.sdd

GATE:
  Quality/security gates
  Location: .sdd/gates/
  Registry: .sdd/gates/INDEX.sdd

SCHEMA:
  Canonical schemas
  Location: .sdd/schemas/
  Registry: .sdd/schemas/INDEX.sdd

## Resource Properties

Every resource MUST have:
  ID: Unique identifier
  Type: Resource type (from above)
  Version: Semantic version
  Status: STABLE|EXPERIMENTAL|DEPRECATED
  Created: Timestamp
  Updated: Timestamp
  Author: Owner
  Reviewers: [list]
  Dependencies: [list of resource IDs]
  Tags: [searchable keywords]

## Resource Discovery

Discovery process:
  1. Analyze task requirements
  2. Query resource registry
  3. Filter by type, status, version
  4. Rank by relevance
  5. Validate dependencies
  6. Return matching resources

Discovery criteria:
  - Type match
  - Status (STABLE > EXPERIMENTAL > DEPRECATED)
  - Version compatibility
  - Dependency availability
  - Tag relevance

## Resource Indexing

Primary Index:
  .sdd/INDEX.sdd — master routing table

Secondary Indexes:
  .sdd/skills/INDEX.sdd — skills by domain
  .sdd/commands/INDEX.sdd — commands by function
  .sdd/patterns/INDEX.sdd — patterns by problem
  .sdd/templates/INDEX.sdd — templates by use case

Index Structure:
  - Resource ID
  - Type
  - Path
  - Version
  - Status
  - Dependencies
  - Tags

## Resource Versioning

Semantic Versioning:
  MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH

  MAJOR: Breaking changes
  MINOR: New features (backward compatible)
  PATCH: Bug fixes (backward compatible)

Version Resolution:
  - Exact match preferred
  - Minor version range allowed
  - Major version changes require review

## Resource Updates

Update Process:
  1. Detect new resource version
  2. Validate compatibility
  3. Update registry
  4. Notify dependents
  5. Test integration
  6. Deploy update

Update Triggers:
  - New version available
  - Dependency updated
  - Security patch
  - Performance improvement

## Resource Dependencies

Dependency Graph:
  - Resources can depend on other resources
  - Dependencies are validated before use
  - Circular dependencies are forbidden
  - Missing dependencies trigger fallback

Dependency Resolution:
  1. Check local availability
  2. Check registry
  3. Check fallback resources
  4. Request human if unavailable

## Resource Fallback

Fallback Chain:
  1. Primary resource (exact match)
  2. Compatible resource (same type, older version)
  3. Generic resource (same type, default)
  4. Human intervention

Fallback Rules:
  - Fallback MUST be logged
  - Fallback MUST be reviewed
  - Fallback MUST NOT break functionality

## Resource Retirement

Retirement Process:
  1. Mark as DEPRECATED
  2. Notify dependents
  3. Provide migration path
  4. Keep available for 6 months
  5. Archive after retirement

Retirement Criteria:
  - Replaced by better resource
  - No longer maintained
  - Security issues
  - Performance issues

## Self-Updating System

Auto-Discovery:
  - Scan .sdd/ for new resources
  - Update registry automatically
  - Notify human of new resources

Auto-Update:
  - Check for resource updates
  - Validate compatibility
  - Update registry
  - Notify human of updates

Auto-Retirement:
  - Detect unused resources
  - Suggest retirement
  - Archive after approval

## Resource Registry File

Registry: .sdd/RESOURCES.sdd

Format:
  Resources:
    - ID: <resource-id>
      Type: <type>
      Path: <path>
      Version: <version>
      Status: <status>
      Dependencies: [<dep1>, <dep2>]
      Tags: [<tag1>, <tag2>]
      Updated: <timestamp>

State: +
